# Footnotes: For element: Footnote area (the rule, the gap and the typography of the notes) and For element: Footnote.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Footnotes · Area and note style
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Styles:
		For element: Footnote area
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Size: 8.5
				Line height: 12
				Color: muted
			Box:
				Margin: 20 0 0 0
				Padding: 6 0 0 0
				Border: 1.5 0 0 0
				Border color: accent
				Border style: dotted
		For element: Footnote
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
	Section:
		Text: Footnotes
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Area and note style
		Paragraph: The notes of a page go in a generated box, the footnote area. `For element: Footnote area` gives its rule (the top `Border`), the gap above it and the typography of every note. `For element: Footnote` styles each note.
			Style: intro
		Paragraph: The museum opens on Sundays[^sundays] and on public holidays[^holidays], except in August.
		Footnote:
			Id: sundays
			Paragraph: From 10 to 14.
		Footnote:
			Id: holidays
			Paragraph: The local holidays of the town included.
